  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Djibouti Country Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TradeMark Africa&apos;s Djibouti Country Programme works to strengthen the competitiveness and efficiency of the Djibouti&#x2013;Ethiopia corridor, one of the region&apos;s most strategically significant trade routes, handling over 90% of landlocked Ethiopia&apos;s sea-borne trade through Djibouti&apos;s ports at the Bab el-Mandeb strait. Operating since 2021, the Programme supports the operationalisation of the Djibouti&#x2013;Ethiopia&#x2013;South Sudan&#x2013;Uganda (DESSU) Corridor Management Authority as a platform for coordinated corridor governance and non-tariff barrier elimination, while advancing digital trade systems including electronic cargo tracking, fleet management, and the integration of customs and port regulatory platforms. Complementary interventions strengthen Djibouti&apos;s standards and sanitary and phytosanitary infrastructure through the Djibouti Agency for Standards and Quality (ADN), upgrade physical trade infrastructure at the Galafi border post and PK-51 logistics hub, and promote inclusive economic participation by supporting women- and youth-led enterprises in high-potential sectors such as fisheries and cool logistics.</narrative>
  </description>
